      "english": "He went to the holy mountain of Skete, where dwell the choirs of the holy angels of God, that is, of the blessed monks who have crucified their flesh in the sufferings of virtue, who endure at all times the death of Jesus in their bodies, hoping for the glory that will be manifested to them, as it is written: ‘If we have suffered with him, we will also be glorified with him.’",
      "source": "Life of Isaac of Alexandria - part 1",
      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:lives.boh_isaac.amelineau_ed:1-19",
      "dialect": "bohairic"
    },
    {
      "coptic": "ⲉⲩϩⲱⲟⲩϣ ⲉⲣⲟϥ ⲛⲁϥϩⲱⲟⲩϣ ⲁⲛ ⲡⲉ ⲉϥ**ϭⲓⲙⲕⲁϩ** ⲛⲁϥϫⲱⲛⲧ ⲁⲛ ⲡⲉ ⲛⲁϥϯ ⲇⲉ ⲙⲡⲓϩⲁⲡ ⲙⲡⲓⲣⲉϥϯϩⲁⲡ ⲙⲙⲏⲓ .",
      "english": "Who, when he was cursed, didn't curse back. When he suffered, didn't threaten, but committed himself to him who judges righteously;",
